<!-- Hotline Miami 2 port: written for the CUSA00368 v01.00 eboot.bin with sha256
     044f0cbb2ca62e7782b31004b40c9f8a71e1d2e8fd981e255c3399743bf313c4. The signatures find the
     sites in any build whose code matches; elsewhere the patch is skipped.

     "Worker Thread Start Race": a job worker (vtable 0x19400c0) runs
         while (running) { queue = this->queue; do r = queue->pop(-1); while (r && ...); }
     (run() at 0x17bda20). Its owner constructs it, starts its AgThread (0x16836f0), then sets
     running = 1 and queue = null (+0x170, +0x180 of the owner), and only afterwards assigns the
     queue (0x16f26c5). On the PS4 the new thread never gets there first; on a PC it often does,
     and reads leftover heap bytes (faulting through "/app0/./") or the null queue (reading 0x38
     at 0x17836af), and the game closes right after starting.
     Line 1: the constructor stores running/queue before creating the thread (the same 62 bytes
             in a new order, the rip-relative thread name and the call re-targeted).
     Line 2: run() waits for the queue: the 12-byte NOP pad after "rbx = this->queue" becomes
             "test rbx,rbx; jne go; pause; jmp to the running check", so a stop still ends it. -->
